    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands the highest score of the day at 82.13. His leadoff role against Phillips offers an ideal combination of volume and a dynamic platoon advantage that exploits his sprint speed\u2014the critical differentiator for our 5x5 objectives. **Christian Yelich** follows closely at 74.33, benefitting from a premium spot in the order and a favorable matchup against Singer, while **Yordan Alvarez** (71.69) remains a locked-in start despite the platoon disadvantage, as his elite xwOBA effectively renders the L/L matchup irrelevant. These three form the core of our strategy to maximize stolen base potential and run production across the top of the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal utility of **Pedro Ramirez** and **Colt Keith**. **Pedro Ramirez** (49.19) fell just short of the 50-point threshold required to displace **Chase Meidroth** (52.37), primarily due to his lower projected volume in the 7-hole. Similarly, **Colt Keith** (46.34) was penalized by a stiff matchup against the 2.89 xERA of Williams, forcing him to the bench to preserve our game cap efficiency. We are navigating a fairly clean slate in terms of external risks, though **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** faces a tight window in the 4-hole against Tolle; while his 56.88 score is serviceable, his reliance on power against a decent SP skill set suggests he is a candidate for underperformance if he cannot capitalize on his high-recency form. We will continue to monitor the weather and official lineups for **Junior Caminero** and **Kazuma Okamoto** to ensure no late-breaking changes force an adjustment to our current configuration.",
